{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-2689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-16x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-2)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-3,1]$, the critical points are $x=-2,0,$ and the endpoints $x=-3,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{4}-8(-3)^{2}=9 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{4}-8(-2)^{2}=-16 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-8(0)^{2}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-8(1)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=9,$ so the global maximum is $9.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-2)=-16,$ so the global minimum is $-16.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/e57ff9bc04fb9d9db592dda6aac9c364fd5f2e6fcd52968627b1e0271919f5bb.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79cbec9405387a3eba5cea86a14fc0dfcd46ae466ab6f494de31e3e74dca385a"} {"question" "q-2689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-9x+3$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le -1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-9x+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3{x}^{2}-12x-9,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-12x-9 & =0 \\\\ -3({x}^{2}+4x+3) & =0 \\\\ -3(x+3)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-3,-1,$ which coincide with the endpoints of the given interval.\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =-(-3)^{3}-6(-3)^{2}-9(-3)+3=3 \\\\ f(-1) & =-(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-9(-1)+3=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=7,$ so the global maximum is $7.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(-3)=3,$ so the global minimum is $3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/2eca6b83a3f99ca87a70e381490e99c98e80a535cd3051a4cdd0740f82de577b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79cbec9405387a3eba5cea86a14fc0dfcd46ae466ab6f494de31e3e74dca385a"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-2698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $45$\n- The global minimum value is $-14$\n- The global maximum value is $18$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)-(x+2) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-2,\\,-1,\\,1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3(-2)^{4}+8(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)+5=13 \\\\ f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}+8(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-24(-1)+5=18 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}+8(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-24(1)+5=-14 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)^{4}+8(2)^{3}-6(2)^{2}-24(2)+5=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=45,$ so the global maximum is $45.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=-14,$ so the global minimum is $-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/9b48417439d0e018250328b92561732dd9f4c8bbec157daf33287b20dac7c41f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79cbec9405387a3eba5cea86a14fc0dfcd46ae466ab6f494de31e3e74dca385a"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-20976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $\\frac{9}{e}$\n- The global maximum value is $4$\n- The global minimum value is $e$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2(x-2){e}^{x}+(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x}[2+x-2] \\\\  & =x(x-2){e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nx(x-2){e}^{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,2.\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1-2)^{2}{e}^{-1}=\\frac{9}{e}≈3.31 \\\\ f(0) & =(0-2)^{2}{e}^{0}=4 \\\\ f(1) & =(1-2)^{2}{e}^{1}=e≈2.72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=4,$ so the global maximum is $4.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=e,$ so the global minimum is $e.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/adeb7eb92f270a216f30cd0466e91d0363c5a50b17053316e6e9f44d0dfaaf23.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79cbec9405387a3eba5cea86a14fc0dfcd46ae466ab6f494de31e3e74dca385a"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-79341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-344460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ is{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-344460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)-x(2x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 1-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-1$ does not belong to the interval $[0,2],$ the critical points are $x=1$ and the endpoints $x=0,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}+1}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{2}{{2}^{2}+1}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The least value is $f(0)=0,$ so the global minimum is $0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/463d11ca52d41491a6184a1d7d39692af43e53aa0fd470324a8f8e999c842811.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-344460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "79cbec9405387a3eba5cea86a14fc0dfcd46ae466ab6f494de31e3e74dca385a"} {"question" "q-344460" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/state.json" "file_sha256" "67211865061a3b662c5a4f7b2a7f3c0152a9873cf02f8f81d2a314b3d3708a23"} {"question" "q-344460" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co